##### Uniform Asymptotic Expansions for Large Orders

\(I_{s}(\nu z)\sim\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi r}}\frac{e^{\gamma\pi}}{(1+z)^{1/4}}\{1+ \sum\limits_{k=1}^{\infty}\frac{u_{k}(t)}{p^{k}}\}\)

\(K_{s}(\nu z)\sim\sqrt{\frac{\pi}{2\nu}}\frac{e^{-\gamma\pi}}{(1+z^{2})^{1/4}}\{1+ \sum\limits_{k=1}^{\infty}(-)^{s}\frac{u_{k}(t)}{p^{k}}\}\)

When \(p\to+\,\infty\), these expansions hold uniformly with respect to \(z\) in the sector \(|\arg\;z|\leq\frac{1}{2}\pi-\epsilon\), where \(\epsilon\) is an arbitrary positive number. Here

